# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.js

# testing
/coverage

# production
/build
/dist

# misc
.DS_Store
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local

# Supabase CLI local artifacts.
# Migrations under supabase/migrations/ are deliberately NOT ignored — they
# are the versioned record of the schema and the app depends on them. Only
# the CLI's local state is ignored here.
#
# config.toml IS tracked. It was ignored because it can carry SMTP and OAuth
# secrets, but it also carries [functions.ingest] verify_jwt = false, and a
# clone without that deploys an endpoint that 401s every valid request with
# no error anywhere in the logs. Keep secrets out of it using the CLI's env
# interpolation instead — `password = "env(SMTP_PASSWORD)"` — rather than
# inlining a value and re-ignoring the file.
supabase/.branches
supabase/.temp

npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*